Logic : 

Traverse the array using cyclic sort.
Check if the current element is in its correct position (nums[i] == i + 1).
If the element is not in its correct position and its correct position does not already contain the same value, swap it with the element at its correct position.
If the element is already in its correct position or a duplicate is found at its correct position, move to the next index.
Repeat this process until all possible elements are placed in their correct positions.
Traverse the array once again from the beginning.
Compare each element with its expected value (i + 1).
If an element does not match its expected value, return that element because it is the duplicate number.
If no mismatch is found, return -1. (It will now execute , according to the testcase provided by the leetcode)

Code :

for(int i=0;i<nums.length;){
            if(nums[i]!=i+1 && nums[i]!=nums[nums[i]-1]){
                int temp=nums[i];
                nums[i]=nums[temp-1];
                nums[temp-1]=temp;
            }
            else{
                i++;
            }
        }
        int i=1;
        for(int num:nums){
            if(i++!=num){
                return num;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
